WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.013 --> 00:00:02.678
"Ark 1" is the first of
a long line of spacecraft

2
00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.270
fleeing a failing Earth

3
00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.740
in search of a new planet
to call home.

4
00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.742
The crew was tested
along the way.

5
00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.543
Lane!

6
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.412
These implants. they give her

7
00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.481
some kind of
superhuman strength?

8
00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.325
-I thought you were dead.
-What are you talking about?

9
00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.885
What. you really didn't
know you were a clone?

10
00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.420
We were able to make peace

11
00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.088
with the rebel
Eastern Federation.

12
00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.790
This is Captain Zed Avega.

13
00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.191
Come with us.

14
00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.894
Together.
we made it to Trappist-1D.

15
00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.295
There's obviously water

16
00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.007
and the atmosphere
is similar to Earth.

17
00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:33.400
But the team at Homebase
has begun to discover

18
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.770
that our new home
holds secrets of its own.

19
00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.439
Other ships are still out
there looking for a home.

20
00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.574
"Ark 1" won't stop
searching for them

21
00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.352
until they bring them back
to Homebase.

22
00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.178
Do not come to Ross!

23
00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.981
Turn around before
it's too late!

24
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

25
00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.759
So set a course for Ross?

26
00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.861
Their message sounded
like they're in trouble.

27
00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.364
Well. exactly. It said
do not come here. didn't it?

28
00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.833
Ian. our mission is
to find people who need help

29
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.201
and take them to Homebase 1.

30
00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.669
I say we go.

31
00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.448
Alicia. are we close
enough yet to get more

32
00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.507
information on the situation?

33
00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.046
Still too far
for planetary readings.

34
00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.157
but we've moved
into range to get

35
00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.615
some readings on the Ross sun.

36
00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.118
It's throwing off some
really severe solar storms.

37
00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.486
Meaning?

38
00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.997
"Ark 4" doesn't have the
long-range sensors we do.

39
00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.799
It wouldn't have been able
to detect the solar storms

40
00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.924
until it was too late.

41
00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.392
Too late for what?

42
00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.136
Solar storms at that level
would have knocked out

43
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.096
all life support
and electrical systems

44
00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.198
on "Ark 4" before
it dropped out of FTL.

45
00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.732
So they're all dead?

46
00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.034
Not necessarily.

47
00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.001
It's possible they
made it to the surface

48
00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.236
before the storm started.

49
00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.647
But wouldn't the solar storm
still be bad

50
00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.905
down on the planet?

51
00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.208
The atmosphere would protect
the crew from radiation.

52
00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.714
Then there might be survivors.

53
00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.287
Wait. If we go.
won't our life support systems

54
00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.745
just be fried like theirs was?

55
00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.581
Actually.
I've been working on a way

56
00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.092
to rig the artificial
gravity generator

57
00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.359
to project some of its gravitons

58
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.852
onto the exterior of the ship.

59
00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.220
Which would do what?

60
00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.331
It would act as a shield
against the solar storms.

61
00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.890
There's a "but" coming.

62
00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.501
I can always sense when
there's a "but" on the way out

63
00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.060
of that little mouth of hers.

64
00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.595
No "but." It'll work.

65
00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.661
Great.

66
00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:10.697
For three hours.

67
00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.865
And there it is.

68
00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.967
That wasn't a "but."

69
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.377
All right. then we'll move fast

70
00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.804
and use those three hours
to search for survivors.

71
00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.948
How long until we're there?

72
00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.440
Two hours.

73
00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:22.108
Call me when we're close.

74
00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.387
Mr. Trust!

75
00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.623
You're not gonna believe
this slab we dug up!

76
00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.959
Oh. man.

77
00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.996
Angus to Mr. Trust.

78
00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.697
Mr. Trust!

79
00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.266
The man never answers his WD.

80
00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.534
So annoying.

81
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.068
All right.

82
00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.971
Uh... sorry. can you just...

83
00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.907
-Yeah.
-Thank you so much.

84
00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.745
OK.

85
00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.847
Thank you so much.

86
00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.051
Oh. that's so cool.

87
00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.487
OK. let's just go find him.

88
00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.554
OK.

89
00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.532
All right.

90
00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.035
-Hi. James.
-You're right on time.

91
00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.903
Eva.

92
00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.139
Wow. you uh...

93
00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:29.475
You look absolutely ravishing.

94
00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:32.278
Well. I wanted to look
my best for our celebration.

95
00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.147
Oh. yeah?

96
00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.281
What we celebrating?

97
00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.016
Our one-year anniversary.

98
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.687
You kissed me for the first
time exactly a year ago.

99
00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.355
Huh.

100
00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:43.823
Is that right?
Exactly?

101
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.359
OK. about a year ago.

102
00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.627
Just go with it.

103
00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:49.329
All right. all right. all right.

104
00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:54.500
So look what I found at
the Homebase exchange office.

105
00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.506
A woman from "Ark 11"
was trading it.

106
00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.175
Oh!

107
00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.910
Oh!

108
00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:05.788
Wait. do... do you know how
many light years away from me

109
00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.879
you are right now?

110
00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.147
That is just so cruel.

111
00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.250
Just pretend
I'm right there with you.

112
00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.518
Oh. baby. I want to.

113
00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.320
I really. like. really do.

114
00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.089
But. um...

115
00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:19.993
Listen. could we maybe save
this for tomorrow's call?

116
00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.261
What?

117
00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.404
Because we're about
to land at Ross.

118
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.597
and I don't really
have any time.

119
00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.032
I just wanted to see your face

120
00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.834
before we go down to the planet.

121
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.937
-You're going down there?
-Is it safe?

122
00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.172
-Is it safe?
-Y-yes.

123
00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.508
Yes. of course it's safe.

124
00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:38.511
Listen. I'll tell you
all about it tomorrow. OK?

125
00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.180
All personnel. we arrive
at Ross in ten minutes.

126
00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:45.184
All right. I gotta go.

127
00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.253
-I love you.
-I love you. too.

128
00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.337
All these times
we've been in an FTL bubble.

129
00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.697
I never realized
how beautiful it is.

130
00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.233
Yeah.

131
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.569
It is kind of stunning.
isn't it. Curly?

132
00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.172
Curly?

133
00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.349
Yeah. that was
my nickname for you

134
00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.851
when we were in the coma dream
together.

135
00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.711
-You remember.
-No. I don't.

136
00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:14.280
-Well. sure you do.
-You loved it.

137
00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.382
I really doubt that.

138
00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.993
Yeah. I started
calling you Curly when

139
00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.352
we were about 20 years in.

140
00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.829
We were deep into
our romance by then.

141
00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.589
-Hmm.
-Did I call you something?

142
00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.725
Yeah.

143
00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.226
Ian.

144
00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.100
Oh.

145
00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:37.770
Ian. we've been through this.

146
00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:41.974
You still hung up on the whole

147
00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.201
it was just a dream thing.

148
00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.812
It was just a dream.

149
00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.580
Maybe.

150
00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:51.017
But a wonderful. beautiful.
romantic dream.

151
00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:56.022
OK. yes. it was.

152
00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:58.991
But. Ian. it wasn't real.

153
00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:02.028
Feelings I was left with
felt pretty real to me.

154
00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:06.966
And I think they're
real for you. too.

155
00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.369
You just won't admit it
for some reason.

156
00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.871
-I'm sorry.
-OK?

157
00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:14.874
I'm dealing with a delicate
balance on this ship now.

158
00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.577
commanding former GSA
and EF personnel

159
00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.245
who just weeks ago were enemies.

160
00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.381
And somehow. God knows how.

161
00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.983
I've managed
to gain their trust. and I...

162
00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.652
I don't want to squander it.

163
00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.799
And being seen to be
in a romantic relationship

164
00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:32.392
with a member of your crew
ain't very professional.

165
00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.860
I get it.

166
00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:41.768
-We're at Ross.
-Let's get to the bridge.

167
00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.572
Report.

168
00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:47.983
The solar shields are working.

169
00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:49.475
Good job. Alicia.

170
00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.919
The scans are showing
no signs of life

171
00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.879
on the parts of "Ark 4"
still in orbit.

172
00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:55.348
It's not responding
to remote commands.

173
00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:56.716
Electrics are fried.

174
00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:58.394
That includes life support.
I'm afraid.

175
00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:00.453
So everyone is dead?

176
00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.221
On the section
still in orbit. yes.

177
00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:03.966
But they managed to get
two of their aft sections

178
00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.200
and a center section
to the surface.

179
00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.326
I'm guessing before
the solar storms hit.

180
00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.537
-Any signs of life?
-Yes.

181
00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:09.671
There are several life signs.

182
00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.006
We may have gotten here in time.

183
00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.099
-All right.
-Let's go find them.

184
00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.968
Kimi. Brice. you're with me.

185
00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.579
Dr. Morozov.
meet us in the shuttle dock

186
00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.638
for a rescue mission.

187
00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:22.041
Full EVA suits
and security batons.

188
00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.586
The shields will hold for
another 2 hours and 52 minutes.

189
00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.046
-so hurry.
-OK.

190
00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.281
I'm coming with you.

191
00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.749
No. you're not.

192
00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:33.152
Alicia might need your
help with engineering.

193
00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.787
Sharon.

194
00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:38.357
Be careful down there.

195
00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.938
Looks kind of like Homebase.

196
00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.682
Earth-like planets were
the only ones selected

197
00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:55.541
for colonies. Dr. Morozov.

198
00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.376
Oh. I'm technically
not a doctor.

199
00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:59.178
More a field medic.

200
00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.247
But people still call me Doc.

201
00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:02.849
Doc it is.

202
00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.626
I'm sorry we didn't get
a chance to talk more

203
00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.450
before being thrown into
the fire together.

204
00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:10.656
Could that damage
be from the landing?

205
00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:12.158
Probably not.

206
00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:14.536
The lower structures designed
for touchdown look intact.

207
00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.671
Does that mean something caused

208
00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:18.464
the damage after they landed?

209
00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:21.267
-Could be.
-Eyes open. folks.

210
00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.869
Let's stay safe.

211
00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.920
The air inside is safe.

212
00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:45.858
We should take off the helmets
so we don't overheat.

213
00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:50.496
How about we take off
the whole damn suit?

214
00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.931
Fine by me.

215
00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:55.334
I should warn you I'm not
wearing anything underneath.

216
00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:58.170
You guys smell that?

217
00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.582
Oh. God.

218
00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.651
Oh. the stench.

219
00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:22.628
These are some
really deep wounds.

220
00:09:22.695 --> 00:09:24.730
Like from the
building collapsing?

221
00:09:24.797 --> 00:09:27.233
More like someone
sliced and diced them.

222
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.002
That can't be good.

223
00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:31.880
I wonder who they
armed themselves against.

224
00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:34.140
I don't know.
but let's do the same.

225
00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:39.345
Doc. scan to see
if anyone is alive.

226
00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.689
Anyone?

227
00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.162
Let's keep moving.

228
00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.369
An X10-class flare.

229
00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:04.580
Well. what does that mean?

230
00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:05.781
Means the shields
took a big hit.

231
00:10:05.805 --> 00:10:07.406
They won't last as long
as I thought.

232
00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:10.309
We have to tell the surface
team they have less time.

233
00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:13.112
No. wait. I might have an
idea that could buy them more.

234
00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:14.179
You do?

235
00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:16.282
-Yeah.
-Don't sound too surprised.

236
00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:19.785
I know a lot about
graviton generators.

237
00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:21.587
Oh. my God. what are you doing?

238
00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:22.931
-What?
-Those commands would have

239
00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.199
turned off the
artificial gravity.

240
00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:26.258
We'd all be floating
on the ceiling.

241
00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:27.560
-Wait. really?
-Yes.

242
00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:30.763
It wouldn't have
helped the shields at all.

243
00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.600
Uh. I mean. I guess I must
be off my game a bit.

244
00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:35.901
I'm sorry.

245
00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.770
We'll have to think
of something else.

246
00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:51.250
They're all dead.

247
00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:53.653
Similar wounds.

248
00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.221
What the hell did this?

249
00:10:56.756 --> 00:10:59.725
Hey. did you guys hear that?

250
00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:00.826
Defensive formation.

251
00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:02.628
Kimi. take rear.
Doc. stay in the middle.

252
00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.740
I told you not to come.

253
00:11:58.516 --> 00:11:58.549
Wh

254
00:11:58.550 --> 00:11:58.582
Why

255
00:11:58.583 --> 00:11:58.615
Why di

256
00:11:58.616 --> 00:11:58.649
Why didn

257
00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:58.682
Why didn't

258
00:11:58.683 --> 00:11:58.716
Why didn't t

259
00:11:58.717 --> 00:11:58.749
Why didn't the

260
00:11:58.750 --> 00:11:58.782
Why didn't the c

261
00:11:58.783 --> 00:11:58.816
Why didn't the col

262
00:11:58.817 --> 00:11:58.849
Why didn't the colon

263
00:11:58.850 --> 00:11:59.018
Why didn't the colony

264
00:11:59.018 --> 00:11:59.049
Why didn't the colony ch

265
00:11:59.050 --> 00:11:59.083
Why didn't the colony chec

266
00:11:59.084 --> 00:11:59.116
Why didn't the colony check

267
00:11:59.117 --> 00:11:59.149
Why didn't the colony check th

268
00:11:59.150 --> 00:11:59.183
Why didn't the colony check the

269
