Why didn't the colony
check the ai

270
00:11:59.217 --> 00:11:59.249
Why didn't the colony
check the air

271
00:11:59.250 --> 00:11:59.283
Why didn't the colony
check the air ea

272
00:11:59.284 --> 00:11:59.316
Why didn't the colony
check the air earl

273
00:11:59.317 --> 00:11:59.349
Why didn't the colony
check the air earlie

274
00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:00.862
Why didn't the colony
check the air earlier?

275
00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:03.456
They did. but I don't trust
any study done under Maddox.

276
00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:05.891
so I'm double-checking it.

277
00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:08.494
Roger that.

278
00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:11.630
5 kilometers out
from the sanitation zone.

279
00:12:11.697 --> 00:12:17.169
Nitrogen. 77%. oxygen 21.8.
carbon dioxide. 0.02.

280
00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:19.939
and 4% water vapor.

281
00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:22.074
The air could not
be more perfect.

282
00:12:22.141 --> 00:12:24.877
Almost like it was
made just for us.

283
00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:26.746
Let me know when we turn out.

284
00:12:31.784 --> 00:12:35.087
-I'm sorry about your brother.
-I know he loved you very much.

285
00:12:35.154 --> 00:12:38.591
He never stopped
searching for you.

286
00:12:38.657 --> 00:12:40.292
Thank you. sir.

287
00:12:40.359 --> 00:12:41.527
We're all civilians now.

288
00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:44.130
I'm not your commanding officer
anymore.

289
00:12:44.196 --> 00:12:46.599
My given name is Zed.

290
00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:48.067
OK.

291
00:12:48.134 --> 00:12:49.802
10 kilometers.

292
00:12:52.338 --> 00:12:54.373
Look. Eva...

293
00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.509
may I call you Eva?

294
00:12:56.575 --> 00:12:58.944
Yes.

295
00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:00.412
Eva. I want you to know that

296
00:13:00.479 --> 00:13:04.049
the EF and the GSA
don't exist anymore.

297
00:13:04.116 --> 00:13:06.585
All that's behind us now.

298
00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:09.088
Yes. sir.

299
00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:10.723
I mean Zed.

300
00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.424
Mm.

301
00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:14.760
Any luck finding
the other EF ship?

302
00:13:14.827 --> 00:13:17.897
-"EF1"?
-No.

303
00:13:17.963 --> 00:13:21.667
We've been trying to raise
them. but no response.

304
00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:25.070
I had a lot of friends on there.

305
00:13:25.137 --> 00:13:26.839
My son is on that ship.

306
00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:34.346
How far are we now?

307
00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:36.816
14 kilometers from
the sanitation zone.

308
00:13:36.882 --> 00:13:40.119
The readings out here have
changed from Maddox's readings.

309
00:13:40.186 --> 00:13:41.754
Air quality is decaying.

310
00:13:41.821 --> 00:13:44.356
Oxygen is down to
almost half what it was.

311
00:13:44.423 --> 00:13:47.793
Carbon dioxide
and nitrogen are up.

312
00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.297
And the rest is just argon
and... and sulfuric acid.

313
00:13:51.363 --> 00:13:53.132
-Why would that be?
-I don't know.

314
00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:56.902
21k. Check it now.

315
00:13:56.969 --> 00:13:58.838
-It's worse.
-8% O2.

316
00:13:58.904 --> 00:14:00.406
Sulfuric acid is rising.

317
00:14:00.472 --> 00:14:01.907
So what does this mean?

318
00:14:01.974 --> 00:14:03.242
It means we can only

319
00:14:03.309 --> 00:14:05.711
expand the exploration zone
out to 15k.

320
00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:07.813
Any more. and we won't
be able to breathe.

321
00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.082
We should check it
every day or so.

322
00:14:10.149 --> 00:14:12.885
make sure the bad air
isn't expanding towards us.

323
00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:14.887
It better not be.

324
00:14:14.954 --> 00:14:19.158
Or it could mean the end
of our peaceful little colony.

325
00:14:19.225 --> 00:14:21.927
No. seriously.

326
00:14:21.994 --> 00:14:23.896
No.
I didn't make it up.

327
00:14:23.963 --> 00:14:25.531
Honestly. I can't believe

328
00:14:25.598 --> 00:14:28.434
you've never heard
the term afternoon delight.

329
00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.937
-Mm. nope.
-Hmm.

330
00:14:32.004 --> 00:14:33.339
But it's very descriptive.

331
00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:36.108
Mm-hmm.

332
00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:38.577
Matter of fact.

333
00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:41.113
I'd like some more
of that delight.

334
00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.248
Now?

335
00:14:42.314 --> 00:14:43.315
Yeah.

336
00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:44.617
But again?

337
00:14:44.683 --> 00:14:46.318
I don't want you
to burn out on me.

338
00:14:46.385 --> 00:14:48.420
Oh. never.

339
00:14:50.189 --> 00:14:52.591
I love you too much for that.

340
00:14:56.295 --> 00:14:58.097
You do?

341
00:14:58.163 --> 00:14:59.598
Yeah.

342
00:15:02.201 --> 00:15:05.104
Me too.

343
00:15:06.872 --> 00:15:09.608
So we should only
widen the exploration zone

344
00:15:09.675 --> 00:15:13.479
10 kilometers out.
but the air is safe out to 15k.

345
00:15:13.545 --> 00:15:17.316
Then we should start
exploring the exploration zone

346
00:15:17.383 --> 00:15:18.851
out to that limit immediately.

347
00:15:18.918 --> 00:15:20.152
I don't agree.

348
00:15:20.219 --> 00:15:22.354
It's not safe to go outside
our established zone.

349
00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:23.622
We're explorers.

350
00:15:23.689 --> 00:15:25.257
We can't explore our new planet

351
00:15:25.324 --> 00:15:27.426
without venturing
outside our comfort zone.

352
00:15:27.493 --> 00:15:30.029
And now that my ship's
population have offloaded.

353
00:15:30.095 --> 00:15:32.998
there's far too many of us
crowded in a tight space.

354
00:15:33.065 --> 00:15:35.668
And hopefully. "EF1" will
be arriving shortly.

355
00:15:35.734 --> 00:15:38.604
We need to expand our footprint.

356
00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.446
Two men and a woman were
beaten today

357
00:15:47.513 --> 00:15:49.048
walking down the street.

358
00:15:49.114 --> 00:15:50.215
Why?

359
00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:54.486
For the crime of having been EF.

360
00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:56.288
I'm sorry. Mr. Avega.

361
00:15:56.355 --> 00:15:58.290
Old animosities die hard.

362
00:15:58.357 --> 00:15:59.758
Well. it has to stop.

363
00:15:59.825 --> 00:16:01.705
I don't have time
to keep breaking up fights.

364
00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.271
I have too much on
my plate as it is.

365
00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:04.539
OK. then we'll find someone else

366
00:16:04.563 --> 00:16:06.198
to take charge
of law enforcement.

367
00:16:06.265 --> 00:16:07.967
Agreed.

368
00:16:08.033 --> 00:16:10.903
Do you have someone in mind?

369
00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.771
I might.

370
00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:15.841
OK. I've cleaned the tablet
and ran a series of tests.

371
00:16:15.908 --> 00:16:18.243
-And?
-Don't you get it. Mr. Trust?

372
00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.678
I mean. the...

373
00:16:19.745 --> 00:16:22.815
dude. I made the biggest
discovery in human history!

374
00:16:22.881 --> 00:16:24.850
Oh. I can't wait
to tell everyone.

375
00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:26.685
-All right.
-Slow down. kid.

376
00:16:26.752 --> 00:16:28.496
A lot of people won't be
as excited about this.

377
00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:31.023
and some will find
it downright scary.

378
00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.659
It'd be wise not to tell
anyone until we know more.

379
00:16:33.726 --> 00:16:34.727
OK.

380
00:16:34.793 --> 00:16:36.304
Well. I ran the
text from the tablet

381
00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:39.631
through every database we have
from both GSA and EF.

382
00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:42.001
and I ran it through
an AI translator.

383
00:16:42.067 --> 00:16:43.469
No luck deciphering it.

384
00:16:43.535 --> 00:16:45.471
And I'll be
testing the material.

385
00:16:45.938 --> 00:16:47.282
-Whoa! Hey!
-What are you doing?

386
00:16:47.306 --> 00:16:48.917
It's a machined alloy.
and it's stronger

387
00:16:48.941 --> 00:16:51.744
than any material
I've ever heard of.

388
00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.712
Machined?

389
00:16:53.779 --> 00:16:55.114
Yep.

390
00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.916
Which must mean that it was
made by an advanced society.

391
00:16:57.983 --> 00:17:00.352
And the composite has an
element which I can't identify.

392
00:17:00.419 --> 00:17:02.154
so it's probably not from Earth.

393
00:17:02.221 --> 00:17:04.456
Duh.

394
00:17:04.523 --> 00:17:07.760
Dude. it's got
alien writing on it.

395
00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:10.562
We don't know it's alien.

396
00:17:10.629 --> 00:17:13.899
What else could it be?

397
00:17:13.966 --> 00:17:16.769
Gentlemen. meet Milan Petrovic.

398
00:17:16.835 --> 00:17:19.405
Felix. he held
the same position you did.

399
00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:21.106
but on my Ark.

400
00:17:21.173 --> 00:17:22.908
Civilian head of security?

401
00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:26.745
And I can vouch for the fact
that he was quite good at it.

402
00:17:26.812 --> 00:17:30.382
I see you were a police
officer on Earth for 12 years.

403
00:17:30.449 --> 00:17:33.585
Tough time to be a cop.
when things were falling apart.

404
00:17:33.652 --> 00:17:36.588
-Yes. yes.
-It was. um. rough times.

405
00:17:36.655 --> 00:17:38.891
Everyone was panicking.

406
00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:42.861
I'd like to take a day to ask
around. do a little vetting.

407
00:17:42.928 --> 00:17:45.130
Wasn't he vetted by the GSA?

408
00:17:45.197 --> 00:17:47.317
If I'm willing to accept that.
surely you would be.

409
00:17:47.366 --> 00:17:48.767
Are you?

410
00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:55.240
I'm willing to
accept him in the role.

411
00:17:55.307 --> 00:17:57.609
As long as some of
his subordinates

412
00:17:57.676 --> 00:17:59.578
are former EF security.

413
00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:01.847
That seems fair.

414
00:18:01.914 --> 00:18:04.483
Then. you have a new job.
Mr. Petrovic.

415
00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:06.752
Head of Homebase One Security.

416
00:18:06.819 --> 00:18:08.821
It'll be my pleasure.

417
00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:12.357
As the colony is
a frontier town of sorts.

418
00:18:12.424 --> 00:18:15.661
might I suggest his title
be Sheriff?

419
00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:21.967
Sheriff Petrovic. you can start
by taking over responsibility

420
00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:25.604
for the two people
we're holding in the jail.

421
00:18:25.671 --> 00:18:28.373
Consider it done.
Mr. Strickland.

422
00:18:40.419 --> 00:18:43.322
Hello. ladies.

423
00:18:43.388 --> 00:18:44.623
I'm Sheriff Petrovic.

424
00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.359
-Great.
-Keeps getting better.

425
00:18:47.426 --> 00:18:48.760
Hi.

426
00:18:48.827 --> 00:18:50.762
I've been told I have
to check on you two.

427
00:18:50.829 --> 00:18:53.165
Step back from the door.

428
00:19:02.741 --> 00:19:04.910
Like what you see?

429
00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:10.649
I just wanted to make sure
you've been treated well.

430
00:19:10.716 --> 00:19:13.652
Oh. I'm treated
like royalty here.

431
00:19:13.719 --> 00:19:15.154
Look around.

432
00:19:20.058 --> 00:19:22.060
You're not very good
at your new job. Sheriff.

433
00:19:22.127 --> 00:19:25.831
Sheriff. everything OK?

434
00:19:25.898 --> 00:19:27.299
Sir?

435
00:19:30.235 --> 00:19:31.537
Mm-mm.

436
00:20:02.768 --> 00:20:02.799
[s

437
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:02.832
[sus

438
00:20:02.833 --> 00:20:02.866
[suspe

