444
00:20:03.034 --> 00:20:03.068
[suspenseful music

445
00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.772
Come here. mate.

446
00:20:06.838 --> 00:20:08.373
I can walk.

447
00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:09.975
Your leg doesn't look so good.

448
00:20:10.042 --> 00:20:12.477
I'll live.

449
00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:14.713
Sir. this is
Lieutenant Kimi Joma.

450
00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:17.282
Lieutenant James Brice.

451
00:20:17.349 --> 00:20:19.017
Medic Olga Morozov.

452
00:20:19.084 --> 00:20:20.762
And I'm Sharon Garnet.
captain of "Ark 1."

453
00:20:20.786 --> 00:20:21.954
Admiral Ben Hammond.

454
00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.889
commanding officer
of "Ark 4."

455
00:20:23.956 --> 00:20:25.557
Admiral.

456
00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:28.093
-Forgive me. sir.
-I didn't realize your rank.

457
00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.995
What happened to Captain Lester?

458
00:20:30.062 --> 00:20:33.265
Uh. she's dead.

459
00:20:33.332 --> 00:20:35.043
Well. Lester would have
listened to me and not come.

460
00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:36.868
Yeah. well.
aren't you glad we did?

461
00:20:36.935 --> 00:20:38.203
Just a little bit?

462
00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.571
Are there any other survivors?

463
00:20:39.638 --> 00:20:41.273
No.

464
00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:42.884
We only made it down
with two aft sections

465
00:20:42.908 --> 00:20:44.309
before the solar storms hit.

466
00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:46.311
so there weren't many
of us to start with.

467
00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:47.546
And I fought next to them

468
00:20:47.613 --> 00:20:49.615
until every last one of them
was dead.

469
00:20:49.681 --> 00:20:50.916
Fought who. exactly?

470
00:20:55.921 --> 00:20:57.765
They've done so much damage
to the structural integrity

471
00:20:57.789 --> 00:20:59.925
of this place. I'm surprised
it hasn't collapsed.

472
00:20:59.992 --> 00:21:02.060
Again. who is "they"?

473
00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.872
We have to hide.

474
00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:16.008
They come out at night time.

475
00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:17.476
Who does?

476
00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.955
-Run!
-Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

477
00:21:42.034 --> 00:21:43.702
Come on! Come on!

478
00:22:03.455 --> 00:22:05.357
What are those creatures?

479
00:22:05.424 --> 00:22:07.235
Indigenous animals
that we didn't know about

480
00:22:07.259 --> 00:22:09.328
until after we got here
when they attacked.

481
00:22:09.394 --> 00:22:10.705
The only reason why
we held on at all

482
00:22:10.729 --> 00:22:12.140
was because my science officer
figured out

483
00:22:12.164 --> 00:22:13.641
that they avoid sunlight
like fire.

484
00:22:13.665 --> 00:22:15.667
So why didn't you flee
during sunlight?

485
00:22:15.734 --> 00:22:17.836
The solar storms
trashed our shuttles.

486
00:22:17.903 --> 00:22:20.839
Now those creatures are
trashing any shelter we have.

487
00:22:20.906 --> 00:22:22.784
Well. good news is
we have an intact shuttle.

488
00:22:22.808 --> 00:22:25.744
I can't wait to tell
Eva about those things.

489
00:22:25.811 --> 00:22:27.045
Really?

490
00:22:27.112 --> 00:22:29.123
Telling Eva is the first
thing on your mind right now?

491
00:22:29.147 --> 00:22:30.649
Wow. man. you got it bad.

492
00:22:30.716 --> 00:22:32.117
What the hell are you on about?

493
00:22:32.184 --> 00:22:33.518
This is a huge deal.

494
00:22:33.585 --> 00:22:36.788
We're the first human beings
to ever see alien life.

495
00:22:36.855 --> 00:22:38.023
Except the "Ark 4" people.

496
00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:39.324
Sorry.

497
00:22:39.391 --> 00:22:40.768
Well. you can tell Eva
on your next nookie call.

498
00:22:40.792 --> 00:22:43.328
but first. we got to
get out of this alive.

499
00:22:43.395 --> 00:22:44.539
You know about the calls?

500
00:22:44.563 --> 00:22:46.365
I'm in the next cabin. remember?

501
00:22:46.431 --> 00:22:48.266
The walls are pretty thin.

502
00:22:52.537 --> 00:22:54.782
I doubt this building's going
to hold out until sunrise.

503
00:22:58.377 --> 00:23:00.245
Garnet to Alicia and Ian.

504
00:23:00.312 --> 00:23:01.780
We're here. Captain.

505
00:23:01.847 --> 00:23:04.383
H-how's it going
down there. Sharon?

506
00:23:04.449 --> 00:23:05.884
-Not so good.
-We're pinned down

507
00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:08.029
and won't be able to make it
to the shuttle until sunrise.

508
00:23:08.053 --> 00:23:10.188
-Wait.
-Pinned down by what?

509
00:23:10.255 --> 00:23:11.990
Alien bloody creatures. mate.

510
00:23:12.057 --> 00:23:13.525
Can you believe it?

511
00:23:13.592 --> 00:23:16.561
-Oh. really? Cool.
-What do they look like?

512
00:23:16.628 --> 00:23:18.706
All we know is they have
an aversion to sunlight.

513
00:23:18.730 --> 00:23:20.141
so we have to wait
until the sun comes out

514
00:23:20.165 --> 00:23:21.666
to make a run for it.

515
00:23:23.602 --> 00:23:25.246
Captain Garnet.
the sun won't come up there

516
00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:26.405
for another five hours.

517
00:23:26.471 --> 00:23:27.672
The shields will hold

518
00:23:27.739 --> 00:23:29.641
approximately one hour.
three minutes.

519
00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:31.076
Alicia. I'm going to need you

520
00:23:31.143 --> 00:23:33.211
to figure out a way
to make them last longer.

521
00:23:33.278 --> 00:23:36.014
Yeah? Do you not think we've
already been trying to do that?

522
00:23:36.081 --> 00:23:37.258
We'll keep working on it.

523
00:23:37.282 --> 00:23:38.683
Keep me informed.

524
00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:40.352
Garnet out.

525
00:23:40.419 --> 00:23:41.553
All right. come on.

526
00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.722
Come on.
We've got this.

527
00:23:43.789 --> 00:23:46.291
I've spent 50 years
studying solar storms.

528
00:23:46.358 --> 00:23:47.959
I know everything about them.

529
00:23:48.026 --> 00:23:49.971
All we have to do is change the
polarity on the Gravelaxacon.

530
00:23:49.995 --> 00:23:53.231
and we can...

531
00:23:53.298 --> 00:23:56.301
Wait. I'm listening to this
as I'm saying it.

532
00:23:56.368 --> 00:23:57.936
It's all garbage. isn't it?

533
00:23:58.003 --> 00:23:59.371
It was a dream. Ian.

534
00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:01.115
Anything you think
you taught yourself

535
00:24:01.139 --> 00:24:03.675
was your brain making stuff up.

536
00:24:03.742 --> 00:24:06.244
Yeah. right.

537
00:24:06.311 --> 00:24:08.647
It wasn't real.
None of it was.

538
00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:11.016
-Ian. focus!
-We need to figure this out.

539
00:24:11.082 --> 00:24:12.960
Otherwise. we're going
to have to abandon them

540
00:24:12.984 --> 00:24:15.187
to save the rest of the crew.

541
00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:21.193
Sharon. we're going to
have to make a run for it.

542
00:24:21.259 --> 00:24:24.763
-Yeah.
-Yeah. you're right.

543
00:24:24.830 --> 00:24:27.299
OK. Kimi and I will
lay down cover fire

544
00:24:27.365 --> 00:24:28.700
to keep the creatures away

545
00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:30.144
as you and the doc help
the admiral to the shuttle.

546
00:24:30.168 --> 00:24:31.236
We can figure out...

547
00:24:31.303 --> 00:24:33.371
There's no way
to lay down cover fire.

548
00:24:33.438 --> 00:24:35.040
Bullets don't hurt them.

549
00:24:35.106 --> 00:24:36.741
Then what do you suggest?

550
00:24:36.808 --> 00:24:38.553
Well. we can all leave this
room during the darkness.

551
00:24:38.577 --> 00:24:40.245
and we'll get shredded to death.

552
00:24:40.312 --> 00:24:42.614
Or...

553
00:24:45.083 --> 00:24:46.985
We can stay in here.

554
00:24:47.052 --> 00:24:50.388
And be crushed to death when
this building collapses on us.

555
00:24:50.455 --> 00:24:52.924
Depends on how you want to die.

556
00:24:52.991 --> 00:24:54.593
Bet he's fun at parties.

