00:25:03.835 --> 00:25:07.172
Hey!
Somebody help me out of here!

568
00:25:18.316 --> 00:25:20.952
Sorry. It took me
a minute to find her.

569
00:25:21.019 --> 00:25:22.854
You OK. Sheriff?

570
00:25:22.921 --> 00:25:24.356
-Yeah.
-Yeah. I'm fine.

571
00:25:46.611 --> 00:25:49.114
-Don't worry.
-I won't go anywhere.

572
00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:50.749
Why don't you
tell me your story?

573
00:25:52.617 --> 00:25:53.618
Got a few days?

574
00:25:56.388 --> 00:25:58.089
I've done some bad things.

575
00:26:02.561 --> 00:26:03.762
Me too.

576
00:26:09.167 --> 00:26:10.268
But people change.

577
00:26:14.773 --> 00:26:18.009
I believe Kelly Fowler
should be freed.

578
00:26:21.012 --> 00:26:23.982
And why do you
suddenly feel this way?

579
00:26:24.049 --> 00:26:27.218
As I said. she
captured a fugitive for me

580
00:26:27.285 --> 00:26:30.889
without my even asking.
then returned to her own cell.

581
00:26:30.956 --> 00:26:32.891
Seems pretty trustworthy.

582
00:26:32.958 --> 00:26:34.593
Are you aware of how many people

583
00:26:34.659 --> 00:26:36.795
Kelly Fowler has murdered?

584
00:26:36.861 --> 00:26:38.763
Under direct control
of her mother.

585
00:26:38.830 --> 00:26:40.198
May I remind you. Ves.

586
00:26:40.265 --> 00:26:42.310
you have one of those Maddox's
chips inside your head.

587
00:26:42.334 --> 00:26:45.136
which made you do
all sorts of things too.

588
00:26:45.203 --> 00:26:48.039
Not murder.

589
00:26:48.106 --> 00:26:53.011
Didn't Miss Fowler help save
the colony from Maddox's chips?

590
00:26:53.078 --> 00:26:53.979
Yes.

591
00:26:54.045 --> 00:26:57.282
And she saved my daughter.

592
00:26:57.349 --> 00:26:58.783
Kelly has changed.

593
00:26:58.850 --> 00:27:02.787
Our people's safety
is my top priority.

594
00:27:02.854 --> 00:27:04.990
Ves. I believe Miss Fowler

595
00:27:05.056 --> 00:27:08.393
could be a big help
in assuring safety.

596
00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:09.894
She could be my assistant.

597
00:27:09.961 --> 00:27:11.863
And you'll take
full responsibility of her?

598
00:27:11.930 --> 00:27:13.665
Yes. I will.

599
00:27:13.732 --> 00:27:15.033
I'll vouch for her as well.

600
00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:21.239
Well. then.

601
00:27:21.306 --> 00:27:23.441
I guess I'm outnumbered.

602
00:27:23.508 --> 00:27:24.609
Free her.

603
00:27:30.248 --> 00:27:32.951
-Yeah.
-Well. there it is.

604
00:27:33.018 --> 00:27:34.495
Personally. I think
the food is much.

605
00:27:34.519 --> 00:27:38.156
much better at The Landing Pad
than at the mess hall.

606
00:27:43.495 --> 00:27:46.965
Is. uh. is something wrong?

607
00:27:47.032 --> 00:27:49.034
Pretty sure everyone
here hates me.

608
00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:50.535
Kelly!

609
00:27:52.070 --> 00:27:53.714
There's at least one person
who doesn't hate you.

610
00:27:53.738 --> 00:27:54.773
Hi. Katheryn.

611
00:27:54.839 --> 00:27:56.741
Come. Eat with us.

612
00:27:56.808 --> 00:27:57.976
Yeah. Go on. Go on.

613
00:27:58.043 --> 00:27:59.523
I'll get us all some food.
Come on.

614
00:28:23.301 --> 00:28:25.770
Why are you outside of the brig?

615
00:28:25.837 --> 00:28:27.639
The council decided
to let me out.

616
00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:29.974
She saved my life.

617
00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:31.743
You might have saved her.

618
00:28:31.810 --> 00:28:35.213
but you killed my brother.
Nathan Stark.

619
00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:39.284
I'm sorry for that. but I was
under the control of my mother.

620
00:28:42.420 --> 00:28:43.588
You should be dead.

621
00:29:13.785 --> 00:29:16.321
-It's OK.
-It's OK.

622
00:29:16.387 --> 00:29:18.289
Wait here.

623
00:29:18.356 --> 00:29:19.424
Kelly?

624
00:29:22.961 --> 00:29:26.765
Why didn't you fight back?

625
00:29:26.831 --> 00:29:29.367
Because I would
have killed them.

626
00:29:29.434 --> 00:29:32.971
That would have just
made things worse.

627
00:29:33.037 --> 00:29:35.974
Sorry you had to see that.
Katheryn.

628
00:29:48.219 --> 00:29:50.331
Hey. do you think we
have enough of this fungus?

629
00:29:50.355 --> 00:29:52.323
Uh...

630
00:29:52.390 --> 00:29:53.458
Yeah. yeah.

631
00:29:53.525 --> 00:29:55.693
Uh. I just want to
grab some of the moss

632
00:29:55.760 --> 00:29:58.630
off that tree over there.

633
00:30:11.476 --> 00:30:14.679
Oh. gross.

634
00:30:25.790 --> 00:30:27.792
Wonder what killed it.

635
00:30:27.859 --> 00:30:30.595
You know. I did a stint
in ornithology before botany.

636
00:30:30.662 --> 00:30:34.199
and this bird looks exactly
like a Eurasian blackbird.

637
00:30:36.634 --> 00:30:38.403
What are the odds
of a bird evolving here

638
00:30:38.469 --> 00:30:41.406
to look just like
a Eurasian blackbird?

639
00:30:44.876 --> 00:30:48.146
We should take it. run its DNA.

640
00:30:51.482 --> 00:30:52.851
Ugh.

641
00:30:58.122 --> 00:30:59.757
What was that?

642
00:30:59.824 --> 00:31:01.526
You heard it too?

643
00:31:01.593 --> 00:31:03.127
Yeah.

644
00:31:03.194 --> 00:31:04.929
Maybe we should go back.

645
